nav-preferment = Preferment
preferment-title = Bread with an existing preferment
preferment-description = Enter the sourdough preferment you have, your baked weight and bulk time. Get the mixing weights or see which target has to change.
preferment-lead = Start with the grams that went into your sourdough preferment. Breadator estimates its peak and works out how much to use for your bulk fermentation target.
preferment-have = The preferment I have
preferment-seed-g = Seed starter used
preferment-seed-state = Condition of the seed starter at feeding
preferment-flour-g = Flour added at feeding
preferment-water-g = Water added at feeding
preferment-feed-temp = Temperature of the refresh
preferment-age = Time since feeding
preferment-want = The loaf and bulk I want
preferment-baked-g = Total baked weight
preferment-whole-grain-hint = For an all-whole-wheat dough, enter 100%.
preferment-bulk-temp = Bulk fermentation temperature
preferment-bulk-temp-hint = The dough and room are assumed to stay at this temperature, without refrigeration.
preferment-bulk-hours = Target time from mixing
preferment-endpoint = Target rise in the aliquot jar
preferment-extra-hyd = Hydration of extra ripe starter, if needed
preferment-calibration = Adjust for my starter (optional)
preferment-calibration-hint = Enter a known factor or up to four observations from the same culture, not both. Use a timed peak or rise at a steady temperature with ripe starter at the start. Breadator does not save the values or put them in the page URL.
preferment-vigour = Known vigour factor (1 = reference)
preferment-observation = Observation { $n }
preferment-observed-kind = Event observed
preferment-no-observation = No observation
preferment-observed-peak = Peak of a starter refresh
preferment-observed-bulk = Bulk rise of a lean dough
preferment-observed-hours = Observed duration
preferment-observed-temperature = Steady temperature during the observation
preferment-observed-starter-hydration = Hydration of the starter used
preferment-observed-dose = Starter weight as % of flour added at mixing
preferment-available = Preferment available: { $g } g at { $hyd }% hydration
preferment-age-result = Entered age: { $age }.
preferment-band = Modelled 80% range: { $low } to { $high }.
preferment-feed-warning = Extrapolated peak: the temperature is outside the model's range or the feed exceeds the documented 20 parts flour per part starter (1:20:20).
preferment-peak-hint = The estimate cannot tell whether the preferment is ripe or has fallen. Watch its rise and use it near peak. Bulk times assume a ripe preferment and ripe extra starter, if any.
preferment-reference = Estimate for the reference culture; no personal calibration.
preferment-manual = Entered vigour: ×{ $v }. The range retains the reference uncertainty.
preferment-calibrated = Estimated vigour: ×{ $v }. Observations used: { $n }.
preferment-keep-targets = Keep the baked weight and bulk time
preferment-keep-weight = Use it all without extra starter, at the same weight
preferment-keep-time = Use it all and keep the bulk time by changing the weight
preferment-mix-preferment = Prepared preferment
preferment-mix-extra = Extra ripe starter
preferment-yield = { $dough } g of dough for about { $baked } g baked.
preferment-leftover = To keep these targets, set aside { $g } g of preferment.
preferment-no-extra = No extra starter needed.
preferment-water-limit = More of this preferment would exceed the dough's water allowance. The top-up uses the hydration entered for the extra starter.
preferment-all-pff = Prefermented flour: { $pct }% of total flour.
preferment-no-time = No reliable bulk time for this formula: it falls outside conditions the model can estimate. It was checked between 0.5% and 20% prefermented flour.
preferment-no-mass-balance = Using all the preferment would supply more flour or water than this baked weight and hydration allow.
preferment-scale-hint = Changing the batch size assumes all the dough stays at the entered bulk temperature.
preferment-time-too-short = No dose in the model can achieve this rise so quickly. Increase the bulk time or change the temperature.
preferment-time-too-long = No dose in the model fits so long a bulk at this temperature. Decrease the bulk time or change the temperature.
preferment-water-conflict = At these hydrations the required dose would supply too much water. Change the hydration or bulk target.
preferment-invalid-field = Check the value for “{ $field }”.
preferment-empty = Calculate to see the estimated peak, the mixing weights and what to change if the preferment does not fit both targets.
preferment-how = The seed starter's flour and water count in the formula. Bulk time is estimated from the share of prefermented flour, using the model based on Table 7.1 of The Sourdough Framework. The refresh peak is estimated separately, without the dough's whole-grain multiplier.
field-seed_g = Seed starter weight
field-feed_flour_g = Flour added at feeding
field-feed_water_g = Water added at feeding
field-age_h = Time since feeding
field-baked_g = Baked weight
field-loss_pct = Bake loss
field-bulk_c = Bulk temperature
field-extra_hydration_pct = Hydration of extra starter
field-manual_vigour = Vigour factor
field-observations = Starter observations
field-observation-temp = Observation temperature
field-observation-feed = Parts of flour in the observed refresh
field-observation-pff = Prefermented flour in the observed dough (%)
field-observation-hours = Observed duration
